hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"18109","Abdussamad narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Amr narrated to us, from Abu Salamah, from al-Sharid, that his mother bequeathed that a believing slave be freed on her behalf, so he asked the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, about that, and said: I have a black slave girl, or a Nubian, shall I free her? He said: Bring her to me. So I called her and she came, and he said to her: Who is your Lord? She said: Allah. He said: Who am I? She said: You are the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. He said: Free her, for she is a believer."
"18110","Waki narrated to us, Wabr ibn Abi Dulaylah, a sheikh from the people of Taif, narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Maymun ibn Musaykah, and he praised him highly, from Amr ibn al-Sharid, from his father who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Delay by one who can pay makes lawful his honor and his punishment. Waki said: His honor is complaining against him, and his punishment is imprisoning him."
